# `pip install .` - a non-editable install of the ai-research service, which is
# what a virtualenv that predates the packaging fix still has - leaves a copy of
# the sources here. It is a build artifact of a copy, it is never what the tests
# should be reading, and `git add -A` will otherwise commit it. Scoped to the one
# service rather than written as a bare `build/`, so a legitimate directory with
# that name elsewhere in the tree is not ignored by accident.
services/ai-research/build/
services/core-api/bin/
# A `go build` run from inside the module writes the binary next to its package
# unless -o names somewhere else, and a 24MB executable does not belong in a
# repository. `make build` writes to /tmp on purpose.
services/core-api/api
services/core-api/*-worker
tmp/

# Playwright and local runtime artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
.data/
services/ai-research/evaluation/report.json
